(A timer parameter reads the timer the caller passed, as a top-level timer reads its own)
To 'report on' with a timer called watch.
    a number called waited is the watch's elapsed in milliseconds.
    If waited is greater than or equal to 30 then, Print "elapsed: at least 30 milliseconds".
    Otherwise, Print "elapsed: only {waited} milliseconds".
    If the watch's elapsed in seconds is less than 1000 then, Print "elapsed: under a thousand seconds".
    Print "running: {the watch's running}".

To 'report the finished' with a timer called watch.
    a number called taken is the watch's duration in milliseconds.
    If taken is greater than or equal to 30 then, Print "duration: at least 30 milliseconds".
    If the watch's end time is greater than or equal to the watch's start time then, Print "end time after start time".
    Print "running: {the watch's running}".

To 'pass it on' with a timer called relay.
    'report on' of relay.

To 'time a lap'.
    a timer called lap.
    Start the lap.
    Wait 30 milliseconds.
    'report on' of lap.

a timer called clock.
Start the clock.
Wait 30 milliseconds.
'report on' of clock.
'pass it on' of clock.
Stop the clock.
'report the finished' of clock.
'time a lap'.
